	"description": [
		"This course provides an on-campus immersion experience for students interested in improving their oral language proficiency. Students engage in small and large group discussion, give individual and group oral presentations, and review grammar and registers of language. They also explore the notions of communicative competence and oral proficiency in order to become more effective speakers. Taught in French. Offered at least alternate years; one 250-level course will be offered each fall and spring semester. Prerequisite: FREN 232 or FREN 235 or FREN 237, or equivalent."
